{
  "title": "AC Arthritis",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/shoulder-and-elbow/3049/ac-arthritis",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Nov 10 2022",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "Summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "AC arthritis is the most common cause of AC joint pain with repetitive microtrauma leading to the development of osteoarthritis in the AC joint.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis is made with dedicated shoulder radiographs that reveal osteophytes and joint space narrowing in the AC joint.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment is a trial of NSAIDs, activity modifications, and corticosteroid injections. Arthroscopic versus open distal clavicle excision is indicated for patients with persistent symptoms that have failed nonoperative treatment.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Epidemiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Demographics",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "more common with age but can occur by second decade of life",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "more common in weight-lifters and other sports",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Risk factors",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "trauma",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "post-traumatic (i.e. clavicle fractures, AC instability)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "distal clavicle osteolysis",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "2",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "inflammatory arthropathy (i.e. RA)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "post-infectious arthropathy (i.e. septic arthritis)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "Commonly associated with individuals who engage in constant heavy overhead activities",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "especially in **weight-lifters and** overhead throwing athletes",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Etiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Pathophysiology",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "AC joint arthritis is caused by transmission of axial **large loads through a small contact area** resulting in **repetitive microtrauma (same mechanism as distal clavicle osteolysis)**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Anatomy",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Acromioclavicular Joint Anatomy",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**diarthrodial joint**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "articulation scapula to clavicle",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "contains a **fibrocartilaginous intraarticular disc** analogous to the meniscus of the knee",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "Small articular surface area with relatively high axial and rotational loads leads to high contact forces across AC joint",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "Exacerbated by articular disk degeneration and oblique joint surface orientation",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "Ligaments",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "acromioclavicular (AC) ligaments",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "provide **anterior-posterior stability**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "posterior and superior AC ligaments are most important for stability",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "5",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "coracoclavicular (CC) ligaments",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "provide **superior-inferior stability**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Presentation",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Symptoms",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "activity related **superior shoulder pain**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "with overhead activity",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "with cross body arm adduction",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "with O'Brien's active compression test (at 90 degrees forward flexion)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "exacerbated with pressing motion (i.e. bench press, push-up) and leaning on affected side (i.e. while sleeping)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Physical examination",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "2",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "palpation",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "2",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "pain with direct palpation of AC joint",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/3049/images/palpateac.jpg",
                      "caption": "AC palpation"
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "prominence of the distal clavicle (osteophytes)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "provocative tests",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "2",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**pain with cross body adduction test**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/3049/images/crossarm.jpg",
                      "caption": "cross arm test"
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Imaging",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Radiographs",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "recommended views",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**best evaluated using Zanca view (15° cephalic tilt)**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/3049/images/zancaill.jpg",
                      "caption": "Zanca technique"
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "Findings",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "osteophytes and joint space narrowing",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/3049/images/zanca.jpg",
                      "caption": "zanca"
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**distal clavicle osteolysis**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "imaging findings do not always correlate with patient symptoms (often present on radiographs without clinical signs or symptoms)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "MRI",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "increased signal and edema in AC joint",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/3049/images/acmri.jpg",
                  "caption": "mri ac joint"
                }
              ],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "visualize associated pathology (i.e. rotator cuff, long head of biceps tendon)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Treatment",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Nonoperative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "activity modification and physical therapy",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "first line of treatment",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**avoid aggravating activity** such as pushing/pressing activities",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "physical therapy should focus on strengthening and stretching of shoulder girdle",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "AC joint injection with corticosteriods",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/3049/images/acinjection.jpg",
                  "caption": "AC joint injection"
                }
              ],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "can be **both diagnostic and therapeutic** modality",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "access to the AC joint is challenging",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "AC joint injections often miss the joint",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "ultrasound improves accuracy of injection",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "most patients do not experience long term relief after injections",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Operative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "arthroscopic vs. open distal clavicle resection (Mumford procedure)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/3049/images/dcr.jpg",
                  "caption": "DCR"
                }
              ],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "severe symptoms that have failed nonoperative treatment",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "outcomes",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "open vs. arthroscopic based on surgeon preference and comfort",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "**arthroscopic** resection has the advantage of allowing **evaluation of the glenohumeral joint and treatment of any associated injuries (rotator cuff, long head of biceps and glenoid labrum)**",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "5",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "can combine diagnostic arthroscopy with open distal clavicle resection",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "open procedures require meticulous repair of deltotrapezial fascia",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Techniques",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "**Arthroscopic distal clavicle resection**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "should **only resect 0.5-1cm** of distal clavicle",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Complications",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "**AC joint instability**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "anterior-posterior instability",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "2",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**can be due to aggressive surgical distal clavicle resection ( >1-1.5cm)**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "aggressive debridement **sacrificing posterior and superior AC ligaments**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "superior-inferior instability",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "2",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "usually iatrogenic due to aggressive surgical resection compromising coracoclavicular ligaments",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Persistent pain**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "most commonly due to incomplete resection of distal clavicle",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "2",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "p**osterior-superior area of the distal clavicle**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Heterotopic ossification**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "**Deltoid dehiscence**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "inadequate deltotrapezial fascia repair after open distal clavicle resection",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "2",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
